  "notes": {
    "semetey-1-2013:p1086:b003:l006": "Мендеге is the epic form of пендеге, ‘to mortals’; the two-line phrase is read as Manas pleasing humankind through all his deeds.",
    "semetey-1-2013:p1086:b003:l011": "Bakburchun and Kakan-Chyn are retained as the printed proper names; their exact referents are uncertain.",
    "semetey-1-2013:p1086:b007:l006": "Күчтүүсүнөн түтүптүр is interpreted as Kökötöy breeding or sustaining his herds from the strongest stock; the idiom is uncertain.",
    "semetey-1-2013:p1086:b007:l021": "Kayypchy is retained as a printed place name, consistent with earlier corpus treatment."
